v1.0.11 — send was dead: the handoff sat behind a Google call that never returns

Kevin: "I see a brief Google authentication pop up but nothing happens."

He was right that it did not send. Reproduced and proven, not guessed.

THE BUG. doSend() awaited writeOutbox() BEFORE building the mailto. writeOutbox
reaches Google, GIS opens an OAuth window, and because the click's user gesture
is consumed by the preceding awaits that promise NEVER SETTLES. Every line after
it was dead code — the mailto, the state change, the UI. Observed on the live
v1.0.10 build: window.open to accounts.google.com fires, then zero fetch calls,
no mailto, no error, note still showing as draft. Hangs forever, no failure path.

THREE FIXES.

1. ORDER. Everything above the first await runs inside the click's own task, so
   the browser still counts it as user-initiated. The mailto handoff is now
   there; the Drive write moved below it and is fire-and-forget. Spec 5c says the
   editor must never block on the network — the send path was doing exactly that.
   Delivery no longer waits on Drive.

2. BACKGROUND PATHS NEVER TOUCH GOOGLE. New cachedToken() reads the in-memory
   token only and fails fast. api() uses it. A 401 now drops the token and asks
   for a reconnect instead of silently driving GIS. token() gained a hard timeout
   (4s silent / 90s interactive) so nothing can hang indefinitely.

3. BOOT NO LONGER CALLS GOOGLE. The old launch-time silent token request always
   ran with no gesture, because a memory-only token never survives a reload — so
   every load asked Google for authorisation unbidden. In testing that NAVIGATED
   THE WHOLE PAGE AWAY to a Google origin_mismatch error. Removed. Only the
   Connect button authorises Drive now, and only from a real tap.

ALSO FIXED: buildMailto percent-encoded the '@' in the address (denise%40...).
Legal under RFC 6068, but several mail handlers fail to decode it and open an
empty compose window. Now strips only header-breaking characters.

HONESTY: mailto hands off to the user's mail app and STOPS. Nothing reaches
Gmail's Sent folder until they tap send there. The app cannot detect whether a
handler exists, so the editor now says plainly "Opened in your mail app. Tap Send
there to deliver it." and, if the anchor click throws, "Your mail app did not
open". "Played." is kept as the quiet beat but never claims delivery.

Verified locally: exactly one event — the mailto, with a correct unencoded
address, and no Google window at all. Entry persisted as sent, handoff line
shown, zero console errors.
